WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.890
Last term I nearly pasted my whole

2
00:00:02.890 --> 00:00:04.410
class list into a chatbot.

3
00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:08.720
Names, marks, and a note about one girl's

4
00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:10.800
health, just to get help writing reports.

5
00:00:11.630 --> 00:00:13.450
I stopped, and asked myself:

6
00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:15.370
where would those words go?

7
00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:18.660
Today: what happens to what you

8
00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:21.000
type, and how to get help without

9
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.360
giving your pupils away.

10
00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:25.340
When you send a prompt, it

11
00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:26.140
leaves your phone.

12
00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:29.430
It goes to the company's servers, and it

13
00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:31.090
may be kept in your chat history.

14
00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:33.900
Some services let staff read

15
00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:35.300
samples to check quality.

16
00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:38.670
And unless you switch it off, some use

17
00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:40.570
chats to train future models.

18
00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:43.520
Then there's the phone itself.

19
00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:47.460
A shared phone or staffroom computer keeps

20
00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:49.600
the history open for the next person.

21
00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:52.150
And a chat shared as a link

22
00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:54.150
opens for anyone who gets it.

23
00:00:55.340 --> 00:00:56.900
So here's a simple test.

24
00:00:57.480 --> 00:01:00.340
Before you type something, ask: would I

25
00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:02.260
pin this on the staffroom noticeboard?

26
00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:04.330
If not, it doesn't go into

27
00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:05.250
a chatbot either.

28
00:01:06.510 --> 00:01:07.990
Think of it as a traffic light.

29
00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:12.300
Green has no person in it, like “a Primary

30
00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:14.760
Five class of sixty, with no lab”.

31
00:01:15.230 --> 00:01:17.930
Amber is fine only with names and

32
00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:20.710
details taken out, like “Pupil A

33
00:01:20.710 --> 00:01:22.170
finds fractions hard”.

34
00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:25.850
Red never goes in: names with

35
00:01:25.850 --> 00:01:28.730
marks or health, passwords, or

36
00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:30.730
an exam before the exam.

37
00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:32.350
Quick check!

38
00:01:32.970 --> 00:01:34.830
I want help writing a report for

39
00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:36.710
a pupil who often misses school

40
00:01:36.710 --> 00:01:37.610
because of an illness.

41
00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:39.460
What do I type?

42
00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:41.600
The second one.

43
00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:43.600
The chatbot needs the

44
00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:45.360
situation, not the child.

45
00:01:46.030 --> 00:01:48.270
“A pupil who often misses school for

46
00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:50.330
health reasons” gets you the same

47
00:01:50.330 --> 00:01:52.290
help, and gives nothing away.

48
00:01:52.930 --> 00:01:53.870
You add the name

49
00:01:53.870 --> 00:01:56.050
yourself, later, on paper.

50
00:01:57.320 --> 00:01:58.480
Check the settings too.

51
00:01:59.150 --> 00:02:01.530
Many tools let you turn off chat history

52
00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:04.190
or training, and some school accounts

53
00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:05.990
promise not to use your data.

54
00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:08.760
Use the tool your school has approved,

55
00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:11.600
and sign out on shared devices.

56
00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:15.540
In my school we added one more rule.

57
00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:18.440
Photos count too: a picture of

58
00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:20.140
marked work often shows a name.

59
00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:22.480
Cover the name, or type the

60
00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:23.240
words out instead.

61
00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:27.050
In the app, build a prompt from parts:

62
00:02:27.470 --> 00:02:30.730
role, task, context and format.

63
00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:33.100
Watch the answer improve

64
00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:34.700
as you add context.

65
00:02:35.570 --> 00:02:37.850
And notice: useful context

66
00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:39.530
never needs a child's name.

67
00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:41.290
Your turn.

68
00:02:41.900 --> 00:02:44.200
A colleague wants a chatbot to write a

69
00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:45.820
letter home about a fight in class.

70
00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:48.540
Which version is safe to type?

71
00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:52.180
The second one: the situation is

72
00:02:52.180 --> 00:02:53.980
enough for a calm letter.

73
00:02:54.700 --> 00:02:56.880
Remember: your words travel to

74
00:02:56.880 --> 00:02:58.060
servers and histories.

75
00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:01.460
Use the noticeboard test, share

76
00:03:01.460 --> 00:03:03.520
the situation, not the child,

77
00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:05.180
and check the settings.

78
00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:07.800
Try it in class tomorrow:

79
00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:10.500
play “Green, amber, red”.

80
00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:12.360
Read out things someone

81
00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:13.820
might type into an app.

82
00:03:14.450 --> 00:03:16.970
Pupils hold up a green, amber

83
00:03:16.970 --> 00:03:19.250
or red card, and say why.

84
00:03:19.890 --> 00:03:22.450
Finish with one rule the class will keep.
